WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
And that is that we actually look at the gifts that God has given to us in our own bodies.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.320
He said, "Each sense was a communication that I left between me and her."

3
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.120
In other words, that God is communicating with us all the time.

4
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:26.440
Her thought was a communication or a connection, or shall we say a wire if you're thinking of electricity,

5
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:32.320
or a ray of the sun if you're talking about that particular image.

6
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.840
So her thought was communication between my intelligence and hers.

7
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.680
We need to give that a little bit of thought ourselves,

8
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:47.520
because if we realize that God intended our thoughts to be a connection with His intelligence,

9
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.200
then wouldn't we ask Him more frequently to let that become a reality for us?

10
00:00:52.200 --> 00:01:00.440
Because if it becomes more of a reality for us, then it means that we will grow in leaps and bounds,

11
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:07.560
because we will allow Him to actually come through our thoughts and our intelligence.

12
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:14.520
Secondly, her eye was communication between her light and mine.

13
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:24.040
All the spiritual writers have spoken about enlightenment, in other words, that God has put us on a journey

14
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:30.280
in which you are enlightened, you're able to take one step because there's light on it.

15
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:36.920
Then you can take a second one and a third one and a fourth one, and it's called a process of enlightenment.

16
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:41.400
So I want to give you a Proverbs 15.3 there.

17
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.160
The next thing is that her speech was a path of communication between her fiat and mine.

18
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.040
That's very interesting.

19
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.880
You mightn't have said that your speech was connected with his fiat,

20
00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.200
but of course we are meant to pronounce our yes to God.

21
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.240
We are meant to pronounce our surrender to God.

22
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.680
Her heart was meant to be a connection between her love and mine.

23
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:12.200
How often we need to turn to the Lord and say to Him,

24
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.240
"I have no love for this person or this person in this situation.

25
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.680
Will you let your love flow through me to that one?"

26
00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.320
And it's amazing what He does.

27
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.320
In Psalm He said, "Everything, breathing, motion, step, everything,

28
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.000
everything was communication between me and the creature.

29
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:36.840
I acted as more than a father who, having to set a Psalm up,

30
00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.680
not only prepares for Him the house that closed the food and everything else

31
00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.480
to make His Son happy, but gives power to His Son and says to Him,

32
00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.960
"Yeah, we will separate it's true, but from afar you will feel my life."

33
00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:53.320
Now first of all, I want to give you Psalm 103 verse 13.

34
00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.640
He's more than a father to us.

35
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.600
And the description that's given here now that God is saying,

36
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.600
"You were going to be far away from Him."

37
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.000
He's talking about the fact that He would be in heaven and we would be on earth.

38
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.080
But you have the second meaning as well, the meaning of the Prodigal Son

39
00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.840
that the human race was going to stray far from the father's house.

40
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:20.040
"We will separate it's true, but from afar you will feel my life."

41
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.080
Now that's actually in the story of the Prodigal Son

42
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:28.920
that He carried this memory of His Father's extraordinary love in His heart.

43
00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:31.640
And that wasn't what enabled Him to come back.

44
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.840
And it's God's love for us that enables us to convert and come back to Him as well.

45
00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:44.280
"You will feel my thought and I will feel yours."

46
00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:49.400
Now there is something that is okay if you love God.

47
00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.080
If you don't want God to have anything to do with your life

48
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.160
and you don't want to have anything to do with His,

49
00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:58.120
it could very much feel like Big Brother is watching me.

50
00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:02.680
Okay, so I want to give you the beginning of Psalm 139 there.

51
00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.560
"You know my thoughts before I think them and my words before I say them."

52
00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.040
In other words, God is within and without, as Saint Patrick put in his breastplate,

53
00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:15.560
Christ's before me, Christ's behind me, above me, below me and everything.

54
00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:20.200
Okay, "So you will feel my thought," Jesus said, "and I will feel yours."

55
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:25.480
"You will feel my breathing and I will feel yours."

56
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.040
Why? Because He is our very breath.

57
00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.240
"You will feel my heartbeat and I will feel yours."

58
00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.760
I mean, what is intimacy, if that's not intimacy?

59
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:43.720
"So we will be far," He said, "and we will be near."

60
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:52.680
"We will be separated and we will also be inseparable."

61
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.200
The inseparable is the union.

62
00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:59.640
"And you will feel my life and I will feel yours."

63
00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:07.640
Okay, so this is the discerning of God's presence in our daily lives continuously.

64
00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:17.800
This doesn't require any liturgical celebration to take place for you to begin to, as we say,

65
00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.640
enter the presence of God.

66
00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.600
If we know the reality that we're actually dealing with,

67
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.360
we're in the presence of God all the time, we can't be anywhere else.

68
00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.080
The divine will doesn't leave anybody.

69
00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:33.240
Because if the divine will left anybody, we would simply cease to be.

70
00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.240
There would be no evidence of our existence if He moved away from us.

71
00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.160
We would just cease to be.

72
00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.600
So that intimacy is there.

73
00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.320
It's a case of entering into it consciously and letting it change your life and transform

74
00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:54.360
you because the transformation has got to be from unlove to love, from darkness to light,

75
00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.480
from sin to grace, and so on.

76
00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:04.200
So Jesus continues, "You will feel my life and I will feel yours."

77
00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:11.160
What terrestrial father cannot do for his son, because it's impossible for him?

78
00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:20.440
Either celestial father did, and this son of mine, sorry, as this son of mine came out into the light,

79
00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.400
that is, we were born onto the earth.

80
00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:29.640
After I myself had prepared for him the residence of the world, well, that's Genesis chapter two,

81
00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:36.040
where you're told that God had created the whole garden of Eden before Adam was actually created.

82
00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:42.040
I placed such a tight bond between me and him.

83
00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:49.000
Him is man representing the human race, that I was to feel his life within me.

84
00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.880
And the creature was to feel mine.

85
00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.400
Now, feel doesn't necessarily mean in your body.

86
00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:01.320
We're inclined to connect the word feel in your body.

87
00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:05.080
It means that we would recognize him all over the place.

88
00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:14.600
We would know the spiritual writers talk about contemplation as a knowing,

89
00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.080
that you know in the depths of your being.

90
00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.160
You don't have to feel it in your body.

91
00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:26.120
And he continues, "And this is my love in general and for everybody."

92
00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:26.920
And why is that?

93
00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.480
Because God is love, one John four, seven.

94
00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:36.760
And Psalm one four five verse seventeen says that God only ever acts out of love.

95
00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:40.280
You can't act any other way, because he is love.

96
00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:46.920
And that's very important to state that, that the whole of creation comes out of love.

97
00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.800
The creation of man comes out of love.

98
00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:55.400
All of God's reactions after the fall of man all comes out of love.

99
00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.320
And if we actually read the Old Testament in terms of love,

100
00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.760
I think we would be surprised.

101
00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:04.440
We're inclined to read it in terms of judgment.

102
00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:11.560
Now, in this second paragraph, Jesus is saying,

103
00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:15.240
"But there is another love, and it's the love of predilection."

104
00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.280
Let's just take a very simple example.

105
00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:22.120
I can say, "I love the Irish. I love the Irish people."

106
00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:25.720
But if you fall in love with somebody and marry that person

107
00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.920
and create a family through that person, that's a love of predilection.

108
00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:31.080
That's actually different.

109
00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:35.240
And so the love of predilection now is brought in here.

110
00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:40.920
So what should I tell you, that's Louisa then, of the special love,

111
00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.520
that's the singular spousal love that I have for you.

112
00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:52.040
Each suffering that I have sent to you was one more communication between me and you,

113
00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:56.040
and therefore one more adornment with which I embellished your soul.

114
00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.280
Now, the aspect of Christianity that makes people run away

115
00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.520
is the fact of suffering.

116
00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:07.720
But we've been told by all the teachers from the very beginning,

117
00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:12.040
from the early church fathers, that are Christian without the crosses and necronism.

118
00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:16.680
The cross is right in the very center of the thing.

119
00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:24.120
And in the writings of Louisa, the cross is there from the very beginning.

120
00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:31.240
And so Jesus said, "Every suffering I sent to you was another special communication

121
00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.280
between me and you."

122
00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:41.080
Now, although he's talking about Louisa, these writings were not for her.

123
00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:46.520
They're coming through her to the generations that were coming after her.

124
00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:53.560
And so the Lord wants us to look at the fact that sufferings that we might have considered

125
00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.280
a terrible, and we didn't want to know about them,

126
00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:59.800
that they might have been a special communication between us and God.

127
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:03.480
Now, I won't go into the whole subject of suffering.

128
00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:04.840
You can go into that yourself.

129
00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:09.720
I will just say to you that anyone who has been through a time of suffering

130
00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:14.600
and they have allowed God to work in them through it,

131
00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:21.240
have come out at the other end much wiser, much humbler, much more loving,

132
00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:25.960
much more tolerant, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

133
00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:32.360
The very experience of suffering is like going through a spiritual operation

134
00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:37.640
in which the on-love and the impatience and all the other stuff that needs to get out

135
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:40.680
is actually excised or operated on.

136
00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:45.720
And you come out the other side much more healed and much more whole.

137
00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:51.880
So he says, "Every suffering I sent to you was one more communication between me and you,

138
00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.920
and therefore one more adornment with which I embellished your soul."

139
00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:06.200
Now, in the hours of the Passion, and in some of the prayers of Louisa,

140
00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:11.080
you hear her wanting the insignia of Christ, that we would actually be like him,

141
00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.400
that we would be covered like him.

142
00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:19.320
And so the Lord says that he adorns us through these sufferings.

143
00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:23.320
So that's the first thing, each suffering.

144
00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:28.120
The second thing is each truth that I've manifested to you

145
00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:33.000
was a particle of my qualities with which I embellished and filled your soul.

146
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:39.320
Now, we who are studying the writings of Louisa can make the mistake of sort of

147
00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:42.440
looking at the thing in general and sort of getting the gist of it.

148
00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:45.400
I suggested that's a big mistake.

149
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:53.560
What we have to do is make sure that each truth that has been revealed,

150
00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.840
that I've actually got it.

151
00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.800
Know the way they say nowadays, "Got it?"

152
00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:01.320
Okay, I have to make sure I've got it.

153
00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:06.120
That means it's gone into my head, that it has been absorbed into my soul,

154
00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:12.760
and that I am now living this so that each truth is actually a step forward.

155
00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:17.800
So listen to what Jesus says, "Each truth I have manifested to you

156
00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:22.600
was a particle of my qualities with which I embellished and filled your soul."

157
00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:28.280
So each truth is very important for building up the new heavens and the new earth that he

158
00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.040
wants to build inside of us.

159
00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:37.160
Now, number three, each grace and number four, each coming of mine,

160
00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:43.880
so he's talking about Louisa here, each visit of his to you were gifts that I poured upon you.

161
00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:49.160
"I did nothing but multiply my communications almost as each instant,

162
00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:54.280
so as to portray in you my various beauties my likeness."

163
00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:59.480
Now, that's two Corinthians 3, 18, that we become like that which we worship.

164
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:07.160
"That you might live with me in heaven and that I might live with you on earth."

165
00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.680
That's wonderful stuff.

166
00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:14.280
Jesus is saying, "As we're growing in his likeness,

167
00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:20.120
as we are letting the divine will take over more and more and more,

168
00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:24.120
we are learning to live in heaven while we are on earth,

169
00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:27.400
and we're allowing him to live on earth while he is in heaven."

170
00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:35.560
So this is extremely important so that we are opening the path for his return.

171
00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:41.640
He could only come to souls who are ready and are letting the divine will

172
00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.480
operate in their lives.

173
00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:46.200
This is a very important point.

174
00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:51.160
And after all this, he said to Louisa, "You doubt about my love?"

175
00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:56.280
I think he's saying that with a smile, of course, because he knows that Louisa's terrible

176
00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:01.080
longings for him are due to the extraordinary love that she has for him.

177
00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:05.480
That she literally can't tolerate him not being there in every sense of the word.

178
00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:13.000
Rather, he says, "Think about loving me and I will think about loving you even more."

179
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.840
So this is a tiny little correction for the one he loves the most.

180
00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:22.520
And that is, he says, "If you stopped thinking about yourself and how you felt

181
00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:27.880
and how things were going on for you and you gave all your attention to me,

182
00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.160
you'd actually go faster."

183
00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:33.080
Now, for those of us who are not at Louisa's heights,

184
00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:38.120
I think that piece of information is vital for our progress.

185
00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:45.720
And that is that if we would stop thinking about how I am inside, how I am outside,

186
00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:50.120
how things are going for me and all the rest of it, if I would just stop that

187
00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:57.160
and give all that energy and all that attention to loving Jesus

188
00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.280
and loving my neighbor through him, with him and in him,

189
00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:04.520
I would take wings and fly very fast.

190
00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:11.320
I want to give you a proverb, 23/7 there, "As a man thinks, so is he."

191
00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:15.320
We would say in modern English, you are what you think.

192
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.880
So I want to go on to October the 17th, 1924.

193
00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:25.640
Again, we're still talking about God's love for us.

194
00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:29.800
Louisa said, "I was thinking of the great love of which Jesus has for us."

195
00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.960
In other words, continuation of the last message.

196
00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:35.640
And his great love for us, I want to give you John 15.9,

197
00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:41.800
"As the Father has loved me, so in the same way, I have loved you."

198
00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:45.800
And then he says, "And that's the way that you have to love one another."

199
00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:50.360
Okay, so we're continuing now from the last message.

200
00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:54.440
She said, "My mind wandered within the eternal love."

201
00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:59.240
That means she's meditating, she's contemplating on it.

202
00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:05.960
And my sweet Jesus, moving in my interior, which means, of course,

203
00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.960
that the kingdom of heaven is there.

204
00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.320
That's Luke 17, 21, the kingdom of God is within you.

205
00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:16.760
And one Corinthians 3, 16, "No, you, not that you are the temple of the living God."

206
00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:20.040
And that the Spirit of God dwells in you.

207
00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:26.200
So Jesus moved in her interior and showed her spokes of light.

208
00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:29.880
Now, if you think of a bicycle, you have the picture.

209
00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.320
And the spokes are of light.

210
00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:38.360
And within these spokes, there is a song and the very center.

211
00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:43.800
Okay, and this song contained as many rays, listen to this,

212
00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:49.480
for as many existing creatures, each creature had a ray all for herself.

213
00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:53.560
Now, this is a new image that she's actually using.

214
00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:59.080
We're used to her saying that the divine will is like the sun.

215
00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:05.560
But here she's saying that each one of us is a ray coming out of that sun.

216
00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.440
I think that's brilliant.

217
00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:12.200
And this ray is all for yourself and it gives you life.

218
00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:20.200
Now, if God has given a special ray from his divine song to each one of us,

219
00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:28.120
then we can confidently, absolutely turn to him and ask him to give us the fullness of it

220
00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:35.560
and to enable us to be able to receive it and to use it to our benefit and for his glory.

221
00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:43.800
So each creature had a ray all for herself, which gave her life, light, heat, strength and growth.

222
00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:47.800
In other words, everything that was necessary to form a life.

223
00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:55.800
So here you've been told that the divine will is actually the primary source of our being.

224
00:17:55.800 --> 00:18:02.760
